.TH TELNETD 8 "June 30, 2026"
.SH NAME
telnetd \- small TELNET login daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B telnetd
[
.B \-d
]
[
.B \-1
]
[
.B \-K
.I key
]
[
.B \-p
.I port
]
[
.B \-s
.I shell
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Telnetd
listens for TELNET connections, allocates a pseudo-terminal, and runs
.IR login (1)
on the slave side.
.PP
.B \-d
keeps the server in the foreground.
.B \-1
accepts one connection in the foreground and exits when that session ends.
.B \-K
requires a RetroBSD pre-shared-key handshake and encrypts the byte stream.
Clients must connect with
.IR telnet (1)
using the same key.  This is a compact lab transport, not TLS or SSH.
.B \-p
selects the TCP port; the default is 23.
.B \-s
runs the named shell instead of
.IR login (1).
This is intended for diagnostics and controlled maintenance sessions.
.SH BUGS
Plain TELNET mode is not encrypted.  The
.B \-K
mode avoids plaintext, but it is not compatible with standard TELNET clients
and should not be confused with SSH.
